# question: Are there alarms containing just technical information, without encoded clinical implications?
# rationale: Tests whether an alarm crosses neither the diagnostic nor the
#   therapeutic route (see CQ3/CQ4), i.e. conveys no clinical implication
#   whatsoever.
#
# reasoning: required
#
# An alarm has an encoded clinical implication if it crosses either bridge:
#
#   diagnostic   its OWN metric (reached through any number of derivation
#                steps, the one no further step consumes; build_framework.py
#                derivation_graph(), 2026-11-24) has an mda:approximates
#                edge to a physiological property
#   therapeutic  its device administers a therapy (mda:administers; at
#                present Dialysator, ExtracorporealMembraneOxygenator,
#                Incubator, Thermoregulator, MechanicalVentilator, see
#                inference.ttl's Technical axioms section), with or
#                without a metric
#
# and is purely technical if it crosses neither. Both are tested with
# FILTER NOT EXISTS over ALL of the alarm's own metrics, so an alarm with
# one bridged and one unbridged metric is not reported (an OPTIONAL with a
# per-solution !BOUND filter would report it; no alarm has two own metrics
# today, p75 or p99, so this changed no result on 2026-11-25).
#
# Two situations reported:
#   - "no measurement, no therapeutic implication": no own metric at all,
#     on a device that administers nothing -- sensor and connection faults
#     and signal-quality faults on monitors.
#   - "measurement without clinical bridge": an own metric exists but has
#     no approximates edge. On a well-curated catalogue this row should be
#     EMPTY: it lists metrics missing their approximates axiom, so it is
#     the place to look for them. At p75 it is empty. At p99 (2026-11-25)
#     it holds 12 alarms that are clinical by any reading -- ventricular
#     fibrillation/tachycardia (metric:VentricularRhythm), ST-II, CPP,
#     SpO2 "geen puls" -- plus the PA/GP1 mean-pressure rows whose Metric
#     column is still blank: curation gaps, not purely technical alarms.
#
# The bridge test is presence of approximates, not reaching an organ: a
# metric whose property dead-ends (e.g. Humidity, a property without a
# process) still counts as bridged here, while CQ3 finds no organ for it.
#
# Signal-quality faults ("Monitor - ECG artefact", "PHILIPSMONITOR -
# Storing in SpO2", ...) are reported here: they say nothing about the
# patient. Their encoded implication is on the VALIDITY of concurrent
# alarms from the same signal (CQ9, CAT1a), which is not a clinical
# implication in the sense of this question.
#
# Validated 2026-11-25 on p75: 16 alarms, all on a PhysiologicalMonitor or
# CardiacMonitor (the device classes without an administers bridge), all
# in the first situation.

PREFIX mda: <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#>

SELECT ?situation (GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT ?label; separator=" | ") AS ?alarms)
       (COUNT(DISTINCT ?a) AS ?matchCount) WHERE {
  ?a a mda:AlarmType ; mda:hasLabel ?label ; mda:hasMessage/mda:triggeredBy ?dev .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?dev mda:administers ?modality }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?dev mda:hasFunctionalUnit/mda:hasSensor/mda:sensorProducesSignal/(mda:analyzedBy/(mda:producesSignal|mda:producesMetric))*/mda:analyzedBy/mda:producesMetric ?bridged .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?bridged mda:analyzedBy ?c1 }
    ?bridged mda:approximates ?property .
  }
  BIND(IF(EXISTS {
         ?dev mda:hasFunctionalUnit/mda:hasSensor/mda:sensorProducesSignal/(mda:analyzedBy/(mda:producesSignal|mda:producesMetric))*/mda:analyzedBy/mda:producesMetric ?own .
         FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?own mda:analyzedBy ?c2 }
       }, "measurement without clinical bridge", "no measurement, no therapeutic implication") AS ?situation)
}
GROUP BY ?situation
ORDER BY ?situation
